(7212928, 1110961, 86447, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by posthumous:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by LydiaToo:</b></div><hr/><i> I''m not sure how to score a sepia image in a black and white challenge with a description of:<br/> <br/>"Reduce the world to a palette of grays, and focus on light, shade, line, texture and form."<br/> <br/>I''ll be back. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>FYI, warmly toned b&amp;w is still b&amp;w. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I disagree. I think Black and White is black and white... not any shade of yellow or red... or anything other than pure black and pure white... and lesser degrees of those to give the tones.<br/> <br/>In a Monochromatic challenge... or Duotone challenge ... this would definitely work.</td>', 'Originally posted by posthumous: Originally posted by LydiaToo: I''m not sure how to score a sepia image in a black and white challenge with a description of: "Reduce the world to a palette of grays, and focus on light, shade, line, texture and form." I''ll be back.   FYI, warmly toned b&w is still b&w.   I disagree. I think Black and White is black and white... not any shade of yellow or red... or anything other than pure black and pure white... and lesser degrees of those to give the tones. In a Monochromatic challenge... or Duotone challenge ... this would definitely work.', '2014-05-05 16:30:20.000000', NULL, 0),
